          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            We can generalize the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/club"} club
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monad"} cartesian monad
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            to a cartesian monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            on an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            Note that the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %em on
            which the cartesian monad lives does not generalize to the 2-category
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            generalizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} larger
            2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAT
            that contains
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as an object.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#the_context The context
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            be a 2-category and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\in K
            an object that
            = succeed "," do
              %em has representable finite limits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-category"} hom-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X,C)
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            and the precomposition functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-\circ f) : K(X,C) \to K(Y,C)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserve
            finite limits.
          %p
            Given morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:X\to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mi f
                  %mo →
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha:f\to g
            is called
            %strong cartesian
            if for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h,k:Y\to X
            and 2-cell
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo :
                    %mi h
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta:h\to k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi f
                          %mi h
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mi β
                        %mtd
                          %mi f
                          %mi k
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mrow
                              %mi α
                              %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %mi α
                              %mi k
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi g
                          %mi h
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi g
                              %mi β
                        %mtd
                          %mi g
                          %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ f h &amp; \overset{f \beta}{\to} &amp; f k\\
                  ^{\alpha h}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\alpha k}\\
                  g h &amp; \underset{g\beta}{\to} &amp; g k }
          %p
            is a pullback in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(Y,C)
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+in+a+2-category"} fibration in a 2-category
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (that is, a 1-morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:C\to C
            equipped with 2-morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo :
                  %mi s
                  %mi s
                  %mo →
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu : s s\to s
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : id_C \to s
            that are associative and unital) is
            %strong cartesian
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            are cartesian 2-cells, in the above sense, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            preserves pullbacks in the sense that each functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s\circ -):K(X,C) \to K(X,C)
            preserves pullbacks.
          %h3#the_object_of_collections The object of collections
          %p
            Now suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            — the weak
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategorical
            sense suffices, i.e. we have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X\times Y,Z) \simeq K(X,[Y,Z])
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+objects"} comma objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1}
            the terminal object of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi id
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id
            the identity morphisms in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\in K(X,C)
            the representable terminal object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Now any monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            transposes to a morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1}\to [C,C]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,C]/s
            by the following comma square:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi C
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi C
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi C
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ [C,C]/s &amp; \to &amp; [C,C] \\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \swArrow &amp; \downarrow \\
                  \\mathbf{1} &amp; \underset{s}{\to} &amp; [C,C] }
          %p
            This has the representable property that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X,[C,C]/s) \simeq K(X\times C,C)/s_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_X
            is the composite
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 2
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi s
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times C \overset{\pi_2}{\to} C \overset{s}{\to} C
          %p
            Similarly, we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s 1 : \mathbf{1} \to C
            (meaning the composite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi s
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1} \overset{1}{\to} C \overset{s}{\to} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1:\mathbf{1}\to C
            is the representable terminal object of
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi s
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi s
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X,C/s1) \simeq K(X,C)/(s1)_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s1)_X
            is the composite
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo !
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mn 1
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \overset{!}{\to} \mathbf{1} \overset{s1}{\to} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi s
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi s
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev_1:[C,C]/s \to C/s1
          %p
            Given the assumption that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has representable pullbacks as well, we claim that the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ev
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev_1
            has a right adjoint. This can be constructed representably as follows. A morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to C/s1
            is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:X\to C
            together with a 2-cell
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \to (s1)_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:X\times C\to C
            together with a 2-cell
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to s_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            to be the pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi X
                              %mo ×
                              %mi C
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ b &amp; \to &amp; a \pi_1\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                  s_X &amp; \to &amp; (s1)_{X\times C} = (s1)_X \pi_1 }
          %p
            It is straightforward to check that this defines a right adjoint whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit"} counit
            is fully faithful. It commutes with precomposition (since the pullbacks in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            do), so it induces a right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1 \to [C,C]/s
            whose counit is also fully faithful, i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1
            is a “reflective subobject” of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,C]/s
          %p
            Moreover, by construction, a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to [C,C]/s
            factors through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1
            just when for the corresponding map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:X\times C\to C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ b &amp; \to &amp; b (id\times 1) \pi_1\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                  s_X &amp; \to &amp; (s1)_X \pi_1 }
          %p
            is a pullback. Now for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h,k:Y\to X\times C
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo :
                    %mi h
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta:h\to k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                          %mi h
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                          %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %mi h
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                          %mi h
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                          %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi Y
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{b h &amp;\to &amp; b k &amp; \to &amp; b (id \times 1) \pi_1 h\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                  s_X h &amp; \to &amp; s_X k &amp; \to &amp; (s1)_Y \pi_1 }
          %p
            The factorization property above says that the right-hand square and the outer rectangle are pullbacks, which by the pasting law for pullbacks implies that the left-hand square is also a pullback, i.e. that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\to s_X
            is a cartesian 2-cell as defined above. On the other hand, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\to s_X
            is a cartesian 2-cell, then precomposing with the unique 2-cell
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_C \to 1
            yields the above square. Hence,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1
            as a subobject of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,C]/s
            can be said to be the “full subobject consisting of the cartesian transformations into
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            %em collections
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h3#the_substitution_product The substitution product
          %p
            Now,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,C]
            is always a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonoid"} pseudomonoid
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            is a monoid therein, the comma object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,C]/s
            inherits a pseudomonoid structure. We claim that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            is cartesian, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1
            is closed under this pseudomonoid structure, i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1
            is a pseudomonoid and the inclusion is a pseudomonoid morphism.
          %p
            Firstly, the unit of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,C]/s
            is the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1} \to [C,C]/s
            corresponding to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_C
            equipped with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta:id_C \to s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            being cartesian means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            is a cartesian 2-cell, this certainly factors through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi s
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1
          %p
            Secondly, for the tensor product we again argue representably. Suppose given two maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to [C,C]/s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b:X\times C\to C
            equipped with cartetsian 2-cells to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,C]/s
            is the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi id
                      %mo ×
                      %mi b
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times C \overset{\Delta}{\to} X\times X\times C \overset{id\times b}{\to} X\times C \overset{a}{\to} C
          %p equipped with the 2-cell
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi id
                  %mo ×
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi id
                  %mo ×
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi s
                  %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %mi s
                  %mi s
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi μ
                  %mi s
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a (id\times b) \Delta \to s_X(id\times b)\Delta \cong s b \to s s \overset{\mu}{\to} s.
          %p Then we have the composite rectangle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Δ
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Δ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                          %mi s
                          %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi s
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                          %mi s
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi s
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi id
                          %mo ×
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  a (id\times b) \Delta &amp; \to &amp;
                  s_X(id\times b)\Delta &amp; \cong &amp;
                  s b &amp; \to &amp;
                  s s_X &amp; \to &amp;
                  s_X \\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                  a (id\times b) \Delta (id\times 1) \pi_1 &amp; \to &amp;
                  s_X(id\times b)\Delta(id\times 1)\pi_1 &amp; \cong &amp;
                  s b (id\times 1) \pi_1 &amp; \to &amp;
                  s s_X (id \times 1) \pi_1 &amp; \to &amp;
                  s 1
                  }
          %p
            The first square on the left is a pullback since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\to s_X
            is cartesian. The second is an isomorphism, hence automatically a pullback. The third is a pullback since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\to s_X
            is cartesian and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            preserves pullbacks. And the last is a pullback since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo :
                  %mi s
                  %mi s
                  %mo →
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu:s s \to s
            is cartesian. Thus, the composite rectangle is also a pullback, showing that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi id
                  %mo ×
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a(id\times b)\Delta \to s_X
            is also cartesian.
          %p
            Note that we did not actually need
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to have all representable pullbacks nor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            to preserve all of them: we only needed the existence of pullbacks of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ b &amp; \to &amp; a \pi_1\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                  s_X &amp; \to &amp; (s1)_X \pi_1 }
          %p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            to preserve these.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#clubs_on_cat Clubs on Cat
          %p
            When
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %mi CAT
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K=CAT
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/club"} club
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C=Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}
            (the permutation category) is the further special case when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            is the free symmetric (strict) monoidal category monad.
          %h3#double_clubs Double clubs
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %mi DBLCAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K=DBLCAT
            is the 2-category of (pseudo)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+categories"} double categories
            %em double club
            from
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Garner"} (Garner)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi DBLCAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DBLCAT
            can be constructed “levelwise”, by taking pullbacks in the category of objects and vertical arrows, and also in the category of (all) horizontal arrows and cells; except that in general such a pullback may not define a pseudo double functor (it may not preserve identities and composition up to isomorphism). The condition (hps) required by Garner ensures that the
            %em specific
            pullbacks needed above do exist as pseudo double functors. Cartesianness of monads and transformations can also be tested levelwise.
          %h3#virtual_double_clubs Virtual double clubs
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %mi VEQUIP
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K=VEQUIP
            is the 2-category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+equipments"} virtual equipments
            (or even just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+double+categories"} virtual double categories
            with units) and normal (unit-preserving) functors, we obtain a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %em virtual double club
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1} \to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1}
            is the terminal object, to correspond to objects of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            This means that it suffices to assume Garner’s condition (hps2) on units, but not necessarily his condition (hps1) on composites. This is nice because in many cases, such as the double category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            of categories, functors, and profunctors, (hps2) is automatically true for all monads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Garner"} (Garner, Proposition 48)
          %p
            On the other hand, in this context we only get that the “inclusion”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s1 \to [C,C]/s
            is a normal functor of virtual double categories, i.e. lax in the horizontal direction; whereas in Garner’s context it is a strong functor.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Double clubs
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0606733"} arXiv
